#RingCtrl8 1
#RingCtrl9 1

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This demonstrates a tire dataset with variable contact patch dimensions vs. tire compression.
#
#Generic tables are linked on the tire data screen for the contact patch: one for the contact patch length (X direction), and one for the contact patch width (Y direction), each changing with tire compression.
#
#To see how the tire datasets are constructed, browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the tire dataset "265/75 R16 Off-Road"  for more information.
#
#This truck and linked example procedure, "Drift into Curb", were matched together since the vehicle's high ground clearance clearly shows the front tires, and the vehicle has enough suspension articulation such that the tires do not lose contact with the ground when they impact the curb. With the variable contact patch, the tire no longer only contacts the road at the tire contact path center, but instead will move laterally and fore/aft as it contacts the curb.
#
#This example is best viewed in slow motion.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: CarSim Run Control; { Tire Models } Variable Contact Patch Dimensions
